# One-shot BBF regen input scaffolds (staging files used during BBF-63+ regen scripts)
# These are tracked in container-only /tmp paths during regen; if they leak into the
# working tree, they should not be committed. Match prefix `_bbfN` and include
# the canonical "input" / "input.json" / ".json" patterns we use.
_bb*_input*.json

# Audit S-01.3b (BBF-sec-04, 2026-07-31): session-handover / external-review / agent-runtime patterns.
# These files are operational artifacts that should never be committed (they're untracked
# today, but accidental `git add .` would publish them).
#
# NB on git's patmatch semantics: `**/foo.md` matches `foo.md` at the repo root AND in
# any subdirectory. (Verified via `git check-ignore --no-index -v` against handoff files
# like `Session Started _ State Assessment.md` and `SESSION-HANDOVER-2026-06-26.md`.)
#
# NB on Windows case-insensitivity: with `core.ignorecase=true`, the pattern
# `**/Session*.md` ALSO matches lowercase `session-*.md`. The legitimate tracked
# files at docs/13_review_response/session-*.md are repo-hygiene review docs that
# are NOT operational session-handover artifacts, so we whitelist them here.
.a0proj/
**/Session*.md
!docs/13_review_response/session-*.md
**/SESSION-HANDOVER*.md
**/*Claude Review*.md
**/*Diagnostic Report*.md
**/*Progress _ Problems Report*.md
**/prompt*.txt
chess_coach.egg-info/
